;;; `open` written as a pattern's relation inside a query's goal loads, as a
;;; relation — regression `goal-pattern-head`.
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The query's goal `(p (open ?x))` asks for a `p` whose value is a fact of the
;;; relation `open`. The loader refused `(open …)` in a rule's `:match` and
;;; never read a goal for it.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `open` is a name wherever the kernel does not read it, at the head of a
;;; written fact, a premise or a conclusion, and under an ordinary relation the
;;; head of a fact the kernel does not read (Q-M1f.66, Q-M1f.571): here it is
;;; written as a pattern's relation inside a query's goal, so the program loads,
;;; and every command answers.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ───────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `f62e34e1`, release: the program loads, R is 4 states, and the query is
;;; answered with one projection class, no row, exit 0 on every command.
;;; The engine loads it.
;;;

(relation a Thing :why "{?3} is an a")
(relation p Thing :why "{?3} is a p")
(relation q Thing :why "{?3} is a q")
(is-a k Thing)
(a k)
(query :goal (p (open ?x)))
